        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Dundee%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Hill Nursery, founded 1855 by William Hill, specialized in fruit trees and sent evergreens to Chicago for 1893 World's Columbian Exposition.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Dundee%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s first tavern and store opened in 1835 by Elder John and Nancy Oatman, becoming the community core.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Dundee%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1843, Scotsman Allan Pinkerton, later famed detective, set up a cooper shop in Dundee.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Dundee%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Dundee’s historic downtown features restored buildings that once sheltered slaves on the Underground Railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
